<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
{{> head}}
</head>
<body>
<div class="grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
{{> nav active=""}}

<main class="shell post-shell">
  <article class="post">
    <div class="card post-meta-card">
      {{> card}}
      <div class="card-head"><span class="l">// TERMS</span><span class="r">EFFECTIVE AUG 28, 2026</span></div>
      <hr class="dashed">
      <h1 class="post-title-big">Calendar Sync Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="post-summary">Terms for the private local UTSA CyberComp Calendar Sync utility.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="post-body">
      <h2>Authorized use</h2>
      <p>This utility is provided only for the account owner's personal, authorized calendar synchronization. The user must have permission to access every connected account and calendar.</p>

      <h2>Operation</h2>
      <p>The utility reads the authorized Nextcloud calendars and manages only its marked copies in the authorized Google Calendar. It does not promise continuous availability; synchronization depends on the local Mac, network, Keychain, Google APIs, and Nextcloud service.</p>

      <h2>User control</h2>
      <p>The user may stop the local scheduler or revoke Google access at any time. Source removals do not delete Google copies without explicit approval.</p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>The utility is provided as is, without warranties. The owner should independently verify important calendar information and maintain appropriate account security.</p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>Use of Google user data is described in the <a href="calendar-sync-privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      <p><a href="calendar-sync.html">Return to the app homepage</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</main>

{{> footer}}
<script src="assets/js/main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
